From 10ee8eaaffcd522e29b75d61fbc2305391b2b3f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Parada <fparada@meatcode.cl>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:57:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] MUSEUM FIX (2026-08-10): in-memory loopback for m2comm
 (Model 2 networking)

Model 2 games (daytona) use the m2comm board, whose M2COMM_SIMULATION
establishes the link via real sockets (osd_file::open("socket.localhost:port")).
Under Emscripten those sockets cannot be created, so the game hung forever
on "network checking" / "this is master controller".

Two source patches fix it:

1. In-memory loopback pipe (m2comm_pipe in m2comm.h) -- an osd_file subclass
   with a shared byte buffer. In native MAME a lone cabinet self-connects
   (tx connects to its own listening rx), so the master's VSYNC frames loop
   back and toggle m_zfg, the FG-register frame-sync bit the game polls via
   fg_r/read_fg. When socket creation fails in comm_tick, both m_line_rx and
   m_line_tx are replaced with a pipe pair sharing one buffer. Empty
   loopback reads deliberately do NOT mark the link lost (only real sockets
   report connection loss; the "rx connection lost" branch is gated on
   !m_loopback_buf).

2. Always send VSYNC as master when looping back -- the established path's
   send block is "if (isMaster || m_loopback_buf)", so frame sync flows even
   if the game keeps the board as slave.

MUST be re-applied on any future mame0.243 rebuild -- both are source edits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mame/machine/m2comm.cpp | 105 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 src/mame/machine/m2comm.h   |  46 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

